# MAX-CONTEXT PROFILE: same model as the default, at 45k context. TIGHT. Read before using.
#
# Trade-offs measured on an RTX 5080 at this setting:
#   * Free VRAM at idle ~300 MB; under a real ~23k-token conversation it fell to 160-210 MB, because
#     llama.cpp's CUDA memory pool grows lazily under load. The guard floor is 250 MB.
#   * c=49152 crashed mid-prefill on a real ~40k-token prompt (CUDA "device not ready" in the VMM pool
#     allocator). 45000 is the mitigation, not a proven fix.
#   * Any VRAM taken by Windows (display on the 5080, a browser) pushes it into silent spill: ~6x slower.
# Use it when you need the long context and you've confirmed gpu-check.ps1 shows nothing else on the 5080.

DESCRIPTION="Qwen3.5-27B dense, IQ4_XS, 45k context (tight VRAM margin)"
MODEL_FILE=Qwen3.5-27B.i1-IQ4_XS.gguf
MODEL_URL="https://huggingface.co/mradermacher/Qwen3.5-27B-i1-GGUF/resolve/main/Qwen3.5-27B.i1-IQ4_XS.gguf"   # the console's Download button / bin/model.sh download use this
MODEL_SHA256=f6bf48653feb854fac1e86fec327bbfe2fa75b2321e53cf0537ef9af86af5a81   # checked after every download (Hugging Face's own LFS hash, 2026-10-25)
MEASURED=yes         # yes = EXPECT_* below came from bench.sh on an RTX 5080; no = estimates until you bench
MIN_BYTES=14000000000
CTX=45000
UBATCH=128       # 256 at this context LOOKS fine (loads, healthy) then fails on the first real prompt: 9/9 failures measured
BATCH=512
THREADS=8
GPU_LAYERS=99
KV_ARGS="-ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 -fa on"
SAMPLING="--temp 0.7 --top-k 20 --top-p 0.8 --min-p 0 --repeat-penalty 1.0"
REASONING=off
EXTRA_ARGS=""
MIN_FREE_MIB=14700
EXPECT_DECODE_MS=23
EXPECT_PREFILL_TPS=1500
